Direct Livepeer Ethereum management

Usage:
  livepeer-chain [flags]
  livepeer-chain [command]

Available Commands:
  account      Inspect accounts or create an encrypted keystore
  completion   Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  contracts    Read Controller-resolved contract addresses
  earnings     Claim earnings and withdraw fees
  gas          Inspect transaction gas prices
  governance   Vote on polls and proposals
  help         Help about any command
  orchestrator Manage orchestrator configuration
  protocol     Inspect protocol settings
  reward       Call orchestrator rewards
  round        Manage protocol rounds
  sign         Sign files locally with the configured keystore
  stake        Manage delegated stake
  status       Read the configured Ethereum chain status
  ticketbroker Manage ticket broker funds
  token        Manage wallet LPT

Flags:
      --account string                  Account address to inspect or use for transactions; must match the keystore account when signing (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_ACCOUNT)
      --chain-id uint                   Optional expected RPC chain ID (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_CHAIN_ID)
  -c, --config string                   Configuration file; empty disables discovery (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_CONFIG) (default "config.toml")
      --controller-address string       Livepeer Controller address (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_CONTROLLER_ADDRESS)
      --data-dir string                 Component data directory; defaults to ~/.lpData/<network>/<component> (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_DATA_DIR) (default "$HOME/.lpData/arbitrum-one-mainnet/chain")
  -k, --keystore-file string            Encrypted geth account JSON file (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_KEYSTORE_FILE)
      --keystore-password-file string   Owner-only file containing the exact keystore password bytes (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD_FILE)
      --max-fee-per-gas string          Ceiling on the calculated transaction fee cap in wei per gas (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_MAX_FEE_PER_GAS)
      --network string                  Network name (custom networks require explicit chain settings) (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_NETWORK) (default "arbitrum-one-mainnet")
      --output string                    (default "text")
  -p, --print-config                    Print audited operator configuration and exit
      --rpc-url-file string              (env: LIVEPEER_CHAIN_RPC_URL_FILE)
  -h, --help                            help for livepeer-chain
  -v, --version                         version for livepeer-chain

Use "livepeer-chain [command] --help" for more information about a command.

Environment Variables:
  LIVEPEER_CHAIN_RPC_URL
  LIVEPEER_CHAIN_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD  Keystore decryption password
